QBIT-20 is a separate, experimental indexing convention. q20 is an independent
implementation, not the reference marketplace. Public rules are documented at
https://qrc.market/spec and https://qrc.market/spec/listings. The bundle and
status observation used to pin the initial rules are recorded in
dependencies.lock.json. The marketplace's scripts are not included or executed.

The bundled Qbit bounded30 verification library is built from unmodified,
hash-verified Qbit-Org/qbit-libbitcoinpqc sources distributed in @qbit-oss/pqc
0.1.1. Its MIT and SPHINCS+ notices are retained under third_party/.
The public test vectors originate from Qbit Core v1.0.0; their provenance is
retained in tests/fixtures/pqc-vectors.json.

Platform logos retain their original notices in assets/icon-overlays/NOTICE.md.
The q20 mark is green (#00FF00), matching the Core artwork's bright highlights,
on black, with italic {q20} lettering converted to vector outlines.

Desktop archives retain the installed CPython license and PyInstaller's license
with its bootloader exception under runtime-licenses/. OpenSSL 3 (Apache 2.0)
and libffi (MIT) license texts are retained in third_party/runtime-licenses/.
Source references: https://github.com/openssl/openssl (openssl-3.0.0/LICENSE.txt)
and https://github.com/libffi/libffi (v3.4.6/LICENSE).
